8. Spectral Regularisation and the Knowledge Graph

Theorem 8.1 (Spectral Bounds for Topological Energy). For a connected weighted knowledge graph \mathcal{G} with Laplacian L:

\lambda_2 \|\iota_{\mathcal{G}}(s) - \bar{\iota}\|^2 \leq E_{\text{topo}}(s) \leq \lambda_{\max} \|\iota_{\mathcal{G}}(s)\|^2,

where \lambda_2 is the algebraic connectivity and \lambda_{\max} is the spectral radius.

Proof. By the Courant–Fischer variational characterisation of eigenvalues,

\lambda_2 = \min_{x \perp \mathbf{1}} \frac{x^\top L x}{\|x\|^2}, \qquad
\lambda_{\max} = \max_{x} \frac{x^\top L x}{\|x\|^2}.

Substituting x = \iota_{\mathcal{G}}(s) and noting that the constant vector \mathbf{1} is the eigenvector for \lambda_1 = 0 yields the bounds. ∎

Corollary 8.2 (Mixing Rate Bound). If \lambda_2 > 0, the gradient flow of E_{\text{topo}} drives the vertex activations towards the consensus state at rate proportional to \lambda_2. Specifically, \|\iota_{\mathcal{G}}(s(t)) - \bar{\iota}\|^2 \leq \|\iota_{\mathcal{G}}(s_0) - \bar{\iota}\|^2 e^{-2\lambda_2 t}.

Proof. From \dot{\iota}_{\mathcal{G}} = -L \iota_{\mathcal{G}} and the spectral bound, the component orthogonal to the consensus decays at rate \lambda_2. This is the graph analogue of exponential mixing on Riemannian manifolds.

